{"shortDescription":"By Avinash  PAn index tracking Latin America's equities climbed to multi-month highs on Thursday as higher oil prices boosted commodity exporters in the region, while a recovery of global bonds supported risk appetite ahead of U.S. employment data.The MSCI Latin America equities index (.MILA00000PU…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Avinash  P"]},{"type":"p","children":["An index tracking Latin America's equities climbed to multi-month highs on Thursday as higher oil prices boosted commodity exporters in the region, while a recovery of global bonds supported risk appetite ahead of U.S. employment data."]},{"type":"p","children":["The MSCI Latin America equities index (.MILA00000PUS) rose 0.6%, staying near four-month highs."]},{"type":"p","children":["Oil prices climbed to a six week high after ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/iran/","linkText":"U.S. strikes on Iran"}}," and renewed Israeli threats against Tehran heightened concerns about disruptions to Middle East supplies."]},{"type":"p","children":["Brazil's Bovespa ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV","text":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV"}}," was on track to extend its winning run to 12 sessions, rising 0.7%, its longest such run since a 15 session advance in November 2025."]},{"type":"p","children":["BRAZIL ELECTION"]},{"type":"p","children":["Investors were also monitoring the nation's presidential race, where President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva was running one of the country's most cautious campaigns in years as he sought to protect a razor-thin lead against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, sources said."]},{"type":"p","children":["Polls released on Wednesday showed that his lead against Bolsonaro had narrowed to a 1- to 3- percentage-point difference in the second round."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"The candidates offer markedly different economic and foreign policy agendas, with a Bolsonaro victory likely to